\import{fnip-macros}
\meta{agent-authored}{true}
\tag{fnip}
\taxon{Example}
\title{Portraits across the lower Hopf point}
\date{2026-11-27}

\p{The three portraits use the Hopf column of \ref{fnip-0005}.
At #{I_{\mathrm{app}}=60} the equilibrium is stable.
At #{I_{\mathrm{app}}=90} it is still stable, an unstable
periodic orbit surrounds it, and a stable periodic orbit
surrounds both. At #{I_{\mathrm{app}}=100} the equilibrium is
unstable and the stable periodic orbit remains.
\citet{Figure 3.2}{ermentrout2010mathematical} draws these three
regimes, and the arrows in Figure 3.4a mark the same three
currents.}

\p{The phase plane at #{I_{\mathrm{app}}=90} is that bistable regime.
The equilibrium is stable. The thick dashed closed curve is an
unstable periodic orbit, and the thick solid closed curve is a
stable periodic orbit. The thin solid curve is the voltage
nullcline, and the thin dashed curve is #{n=n_{\infty}(V)}.}

